        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Lake sediment is sediment which covers the bottom of a lake. Lake sediments are comprised mainly of clastic material (sediment of clay, silt, and sand sizes), organic debris, chemical precipitates, or combinations of these.</owl:annotatedTarget>
