        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The group of nerve cell bodies that conveys auditory sensation from the organ of Corti to the hindbrain and resides on the cochlear part of the vestibulocochlear nerve (eighth cranial nerve)[MP]. distributed to the hair cells of the spiral organ. The cochlear fibers arise in bipolar cells in the spiral ganglion in the modiolus.</obo:IAO_0000115>
