        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Anatomical organ component composed of a double layer of serous membrane that suspends a viscus from the body wall or connects adjacent viscera and in doing so conveys blood vessels, lymphatics and nerves to and from the viscera. Examples: greater omentum, broad ligament of uterus, sigmoid mesocolon.</obo:IAO_0000115>
