        <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Grasses or graminoids are monocotyledonous from Poales Order, usually herbaceos plants with narrow leaves growing from the base. They include some of the most versatile plant life-forms and became widespread toward the end of the Cretaceous period. Source: wikipedia.org; eol.org</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Grass</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


